falling asleep to the sound of a distant train, and waking up as its conductor.

walking uphill for so long that you've ceased to notice the incline, until you finally turn around and see the view.

seeing your worst fear brought to life, standing on its own two feet in front of you, as you meet one another's gaze not with anger or denial or contempt, but simple acknowledgement of the other as an eequal.

a finger held to the lips like the blizzard that blankets city streets into a sweet, fleeting silence.

the first moment of the last bite of the best meal you've ever had.
